      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit of a Ford F-150's auto transmission could be caused by several issues. Common culprits include worn seals within the transmission that fail to maintain consistent hydraulic pressure, a clogged transmission pan, faulty valve body which manages oil flow and hydraulic pressure, or issues with the transmission pump, such as wear or internal blockages. Further diagnostic imaging such as a transmission flow test or inspection of the transmission fluid may be necessary to pinpoint the exact problem.",
